  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> be a differentiable function at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;equals:"
  },
